---
description: Rules for building the VitalCap interactive BCP dependency demo
globs: ["public/bcp-*.js", "public/data/**", "public/index.html", "public/styles.css", "public/app.js", "tests/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- The source of truth is VITALCAP_INTERACTIVE_SPEC.md in the repo root. Re-read it before each milestone.
- Work one milestone at a time; stop and wait for the user's "go" before the next.
- The user is a beginner: explain changes in plain language and give exact commands to run.
- Plain HTML/CSS/JS only: no frameworks, bundlers or TypeScript. Keep calculation logic as pure functions in public/bcp-engine.js (no DOM access), tested with node --test.
- Do not remove or break existing sections of public/index.html; only add the new #dependencies section and append styles.
- Never write historical incident facts from memory; leave TODO placeholders with a required sourceUrl.
- Do not add "illustrative" labels to the demo. Every panel shows its data-source badge (Application Repository, Workforce System, Third-Party Risk Management, BIA register).
- The demo is a bank: Department -> Process -> Application dropdowns; disruptions must be traced down to named teams and people.
- Ask before installing any package not named in the spec.
